   "subject": "Re: Satorra-Bentler 2010 test statistic",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I tried this again with earlier lavaan versions and I still got a negative test statistic. Versions 0.5-20 and 0.5-18 both gave the same result as 0.5-22.<div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t know if the warnings about estimated variances being negative and covariance matrices not being positive definite have anything to do with this.<div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "iOck_pPYCQAJ",
   "from": "yros...@gmail.com",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2017-08-28T14:58:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: Satorra-Bentler 2010 test statistic",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>The reason for the negative test statistic turned out to be: the information matrix of the M10 model (the model H1, where we plug in the estimates of H0) was not positive definite. This can result in negative test statistics.<br><br>In lavaan dev 0.6-1.1146, a check is now in place, resulting in a warning message, and no test statistic.<br><br>Yves.<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
